<!--CLI Documentation — ValidateCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.ValidateCommand-->
<clidocumentation:ValidateCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:valdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    blockml validate specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        blockml validate [file] [--all] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b] [--verbose]
    
        Single file: parse + compileBmlToBom against the full project registry.
        Default (no file, no --all): semantic-validate project sources only (this package srcDir
        plus local packages/* BlockML modules). npm libraries stay on the registry for resolve.
        --all: semantic-validate every document in the registry, including npm.
        --verbose: print srcDir, seeds, search index, graph, validate set, registry files
        (before diagnostics).
    
        Validity is parse + semantic validate only. XSD is a render target
        (blockml compile xsd) and is not consulted.
    
        file and --all together → exit 2 (CLI10).
        No target bootstrap. No output files written (CLI11).
        Exit 0 on success; 1 on diagnostic errors; 2 on config errors.
        After diagnostics, always: Validation succeeded|failed. Tested N block(s), M with errors, W warning(s), R recommendation(s).
        M is unique filePaths among printed error diagnostics (parse + semantic), not only semantic validate() failures.
    
    Printed help:
    Usage: blockml validate [--all] [<file>] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b] [--verbose]
           blockml validate --help
    
    When: check the model after edits. Ordinary project work.
    
    Default (no file, no --all): semantic-validate project sources only (this package srcDir plus local packages/*). npm libraries stay on the registry for resolve.
    --all: semantic-validate every document in the registry, including npm. Do not use --all as the default after every edit.
    Single file: parse + compileBmlToBom against the full project registry.
    file and --all together exit 2.
    
    Validity is parse + semantic validate only. XSD is a render target (compile xsd) and is not consulted.
    No target bootstrap. No output files written.
    
    Flags:
      --all         entire reachable corpus, including npm
      --verbose     print srcDir, seeds, index, graph, validate set, registry files
      --src / --libraries   corpus overrides
    
    Exit 0 on success; 1 on diagnostic errors; 2 on config errors.
    After diagnostics: Validation succeeded|failed. Tested N block(s), M with errors, W warning(s), R recommendation(s).
    Do not ignore validation errors caused by your changes.
    
    Related: search, inspect.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Configuration" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="valdocumentation:ValidityContract" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidocumentation:ValidateCommand>
